@* TextField's Overview, written by hand, after Button's: a sentence and an example per section,
   code alone where a preview would show nothing new (types change the keyboard, not the look).
   Mode support, accessibility and the parameters follow; the API page has the full reference. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and hints</Heading>
<TextBlock>A field's label comes from the model: its <Code>[Display(Name)]</Code>, or the property name in words. <Code>[Required]</Code> adds a required mark. To replace the label, set <Code>Label</Code>; to add help under the field, set <Code>Hint</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-labels" />

<Heading Level="2">Types</Heading>
<TextBlock>A field's type sets the on-screen keyboard, and for email and URL, the browser's check. To make the field an email, phone, URL, search or password field, set <Code>Type</Code>. The type defaults from <Code>[EmailAddress]</Code>, <Code>[Phone]</Code>, <Code>[Url]</Code> and <Code>[DataType(DataType.Password)]</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Types</Code>

<Heading Level="2">Passwords</Heading>
<TextBlock>Once <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">IzzyBlazor's script</Anchor> runs, a password field gets a button that shows and hides the password. To leave the button out, set <Code>Reveal="false"</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-password" />

<Heading Level="2">Icons</Heading>
<TextBlock>To show an icon inside the field, set <Code>StartIcon</Code> or <Code>EndIcon</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-icons" />

<Heading Level="2">A clear button</Heading>
<TextBlock>A clear button empties the field. It shows while the field has a value. Set <Code>Clearable</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-clearable" />
<TextBlock>Every field whose value can be empty has <Code>Clearable</Code>. A <Code>Select</Code> clears back to its <Code>Placeholder</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Add-ons</Heading>
<TextBlock>Add-ons attach text, a <Anchor Href="docs/components/select">Select</Anchor> or a button to the side of the field. Set <Code>StartAddon</Code> or <Code>EndAddon</Code>. A submit button in an add-on posts the form, so a search box works with JavaScript off.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-addons" />

<Heading Level="2">Validation</Heading>
<TextBlock>A field's rules come from the model's attributes. Before the form post, the browser checks required, length, range, email and URL, with your <Code>ErrorMessage</Code>. After it, the server checks every rule and shows its messages under the field.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-validation" />

<Heading Level="2">Sizes, read-only and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>To line the field up with buttons and other fields, set <Code>Size</Code>. A read-only field posts its value, but the user can't change it; set <Code>ReadOnly</Code>. A disabled field doesn't post; set <Code>Disabled</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="text-field-states" />
<TextBlock>Before saving a read-only or disabled value from a form post, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#disabled-fields-and-form-posts">Disabled fields and form posts</Anchor> and <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#values-a-form-post-can-change">Values a form post can change</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<Heading Level="2">See also</Heading>
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor>: posts on static pages and validates on interactive ones.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/text-area">TextArea</Anchor>: several lines, growing and counting.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/number-field">NumberField</Anchor>: numbers, with stepper buttons.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/field-frame">FieldFrame</Anchor>: the same label, hint and errors around a control of your own.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/common/style-props">Style props</Anchor>: <Code>Width</Code>, <Code>Grow</Code> and margins on the whole field.</ListItem>
    <TroubleshootingLinks Component="TextField" />
</List>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @* Label, type and limits from the model's attributes. *@
        <TextField @bind-Value="Model.Email" />

        @* Your own label and a hint. *@
        <TextField @bind-Value="Model.Dept" Label="Department" Hint="On your profile." />

        @* Text attached to the field. *@
        <TextField @bind-Value="Model.Website">
            <StartAddon>https://</StartAddon>
        </TextField>
        """;

    private const string Types = """
        @* [Phone] on the property: type="tel". *@
        <TextField @bind-Value="Model.Phone" />

        <TextField @bind-Value="Model.Query" Type="TextFieldType.Search" />
        """;
}
